#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/blindness/_index.adoc:326
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "ed"
msgstr "ed"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/blindness/_index.adoc:331
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man:ed[1] utility is a line-oriented text editor used to create, view, "
"and modify text files.  It is included by default in a standard FreeBSD "
"installation.  To start the editor, run:"
msgstr "man:ed[1] 是一款面向行的文本编辑器，可用于创建、查看和修改文本文件。它默认包含在标准 FreeBSD 安装中。运行以下命令启动编辑器："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/blindness/_index.adoc:335
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% ed\n"
msgstr "% ed\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/blindness/_index.adoc:339
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ed is a powerful editor.  Refer to its manual page man:ed[1] for a complete "
"overview of its features and command syntax."
msgstr "ed 是一款功能强大的编辑器。有关其功能和命令语法的完整概述，请参阅手册页 man:ed[1]。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/blindness/_index.adoc:344
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ed does not support multibyte characters and may not handle non-ASCII text "
"correctly.  Alternatively, consider using crossref:blindness[edbrowse,"
"edbrowse], which offers robust text editing features in addition to its "
"browsing capabilities."
msgstr "ed 不支持多字节字符，可能无法正确处理非 ASCII 文本。也可以考虑使用 crossref:blindness[edbrowse,edbrowse]，它除了具备浏览功能外，还提供了强大的文本编辑功能。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/accessibility/blindness/_index.adoc:347
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
